{
  /*
   * Type-checks the SUITES (#668 C1). tsconfig.json's `include` is ["src", ...]
   * only, so until now every file under tests/ — 190-odd of them — was compiled
   * by esbuild at vitest startup, which strips types without checking them. A
   * test could assert against a shape the code no longer has and still go
   * green.
   *
   * This is a separate config rather than a wider `include` on tsconfig.json
   * because that project is composite and emits dist/: pulling tests/ into it
   * would ship the suites to consumers.
   *
   * The overrides below are all consequences of extending a composite project:
   *   composite/declaration/declarationMap — a composite project may not
   *     disable emit, and emit is exactly what this config wants to skip.
   *   rootDir — inherited as "src", which makes every tests/ file an error
   *     ("not under rootDir") before any real checking happens.
   *   tsBuildInfoFile — its own path, so incremental state never collides with
   *     the build's.
   *   types — the suites need node builtins (tests/setup.ts imports
   *     node:crypto, syncRealtimeTables.test.ts reads a migration off disk) and
   *     vitest's globals, which vitest.config.ts turns on rather than importing.
   */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "noEmit": true,
    "incremental": true,
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.test.tsbuildinfo",
    "rootDir": ".",
    "types": ["react", "node", "vitest/globals"]
  },
  "include": ["src", "src/**/*.json", "tests"],

  /*
   * BASELINE (#668 C1) — the 12 suites that did not compile the first time a
   * type checker was ever pointed at tests/. 15 errors total, measured before
   * this list was written; the breakdown is in the PR that added it.
   *
   * Same shape and same discipline as the eslint baseline in eslint.config.js:
   * a per-file quarantine, not a rule relaxed everywhere. Turning the gate
   * on only once all 15 were fixed would mean the other 180 suites keep
   * drifting in the meantime; this way every suite outside the list is checked
   * from today and a NEW broken one fails CI.
   *
   * None of these are config problems. They are real drift the suites had been
   * hiding — fixtures missing a field the type gained (TrashViewLabels.close,
   * WikiTag.icon), a patch object naming a property its type dropped
   * (SeriesEditablePatch.memo), a status string that is no longer a TaskStatus,
   * and five @ts-expect-error directives guarding errors that no longer happen.
   * Fixing them changes assertions, so it belongs in its own PR, not the one
   * that installs the net.
   *
   * DO NOT APPEND TO THIS LIST. Deleting a line is how a fix gets recorded.
   */
  "exclude": [
    "tests/appShell.test.tsx",
    "tests/appShellSoftKeyboard.test.tsx",
    "tests/bottomBarActions.test.tsx",
    "tests/components.test.tsx",
    "tests/connectGraphModel.test.ts",
    "tests/eventEditorSave.test.ts",
    "tests/notesUnifiedTrashLock.test.tsx",
    "tests/reconcileRoutine.test.tsx",
    "tests/trashView.test.tsx",
    "tests/treeMovementReorderOnly.test.ts",
    "tests/undoRedoManager.test.ts",
    "tests/useMediaQuery.test.ts"
  ]
}
